+   * (3574 and 7075 against 659 and 460 on an SVT-AV1 clip).
+   *
+   * That reasoning was wrong, and the regression suite said so: tests 19 and 31 read per
+   * superblock bits at frames 2 and 6 of the reference clip, and both of those are re-shown
+   * frames. What the decoder hands back is the block data of the picture being re-shown - a hidden
+   * alt-ref coded in an earlier packet, which is exactly why its bit count is unlike its
+   * neighbours and much larger. That is real data about the picture on screen, and suppressing it
+   * would have removed the only statistics those frames have.
+   *
+   * The bitstream dump still labels the frame (see getItemDataDump), so the five byte packet and
+   * these numbers no longer look like a contradiction.
+   */
